  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Georgia SPS Inst Byggnad</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Georgia food safety inst building - GEO food safety inst building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building and institutional support to the Georgian National  Food Agency implemented by the Swedish Board of Agriculture as lead.  The purpose is to assist Georgia adopting to EU requirements to be    able to conclude a deep and comprehensive free trade agreement with   the EU.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den 12 september 2011 startade Sida projektet &#x201c;Cooperation between the Swedish Board of Agriculture and the Georgian National Food Agency&#x201d;.  Projektet genomf&#xf6;rs av svenska Jordbruksverket i samarbete med georgiska Livsmedelsverket.

Projektets m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla att system f&#xf6;r livsmedelss&#xe4;kerhet, i linje med EU: s och internationella standarder, kan etableras och uppr&#xe4;tth&#xe5;llas i Georgien. Genom att uppn&#xe5; m&#xe5;let kommer projektet att bidra till att utveckla jordbruket och livsmedelsmarknaden, samt minimera h&#xe4;lsoriskerna f&#xf6;r den georgiska befolkningen.

Projektet syftar till att st&#xf6;dja och bygga upp kapacitet p&#xe5; georgiska Livsmedelsverket genom att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra administration och f&#xf6;rvaltning, s&#xe4;kerhet i livsmedelsproduktion genom effektiva inspektionssystem, veterin&#xe4;rtj&#xe4;nster, samt metoder f&#xf6;r att reagera snabbt i n&#xf6;dsituationer relaterade till p&#xe5; livsmedelss&#xe4;kerhet. Sida godk&#xe4;nner att budgetposten &#xd6;vrigt i budgeten anv&#xe4;nds f&#xf6;r kostnadsf&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngningen.

Mot slutet av projektet efterfr&#xe5;gades en kostnadsf&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngning fram till slutet av juni 2015 som skulle g&#xf6;ra det m&#xf6;jligt att avsluta vissa utbildningar och aktiviteter f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla kontinuiteten i processen, vilket Sida bed&#xf6;mt vara rimligt f&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; &#xf6;nskade resultat.

--


The project &#x201c;Cooperation between the Swedish Board of Agriculture and the Georgian National Food Agency&#x201d;  started in September 12, 2011. The project implementation partner is Swedish Board of Agriculture. The cooperation partner is Georgia National Food Agency.
 
The project objective is to ensure that a solid food safety system, in line with the EU and international standards, can be established and sustained in Georgia. Achieving the objective will help to develop agricultural and food market and minimizing health hazards to the Georgian population. The project aims to achieve the objective supporting and building capacity of Georgian National Food Agency in improving its administration and management, safety and securing of the food supply through efficient inspection systems, veterinary services, methods for responding quickly to food safety related emergencies.

The project closer to its end requested cost extension until the end of June 2015 that would allow it to finish some trainings and activities to ensure continuity of the process. The relevant budget was submitted to Sida. Sida approves that the Miscellaneous budget line in the budget is used for the cost extension. The cost extension request was supported by the beneficiary organization National Food Agency. 

In order to complete the project and achieve results set up by the project initially it is suggested to grant the project cost extension.</narrative>
  </description>
